essels to each contain a specific ingredient, and each vessel must be grasped, filled, and released in turn.: Endorse concrete grasp-fill-release sequences that directly satisfy each goal condition, and trust the valid-actions list to confirm each next step; reject think/no-op outputs that stall progress.', 'When When a multi-step goal requires retrieving and processing several items from a container, and each item must be handled and returned before the next.: Continue endorsing concrete fetch-process-put-away sequences that advance the goal, and reject think/no-op outputs that stall progress; trust the valid-actions list when a target seems unavailable.'], 'finalizer': ['When When a stacking goal requires rearranging multiple blocks and the current configuration blocks direct placement of a target block.: Before each manipulation, run check-valid-actions to confirm the exact source-destination pair is legal; if the desired placement is invalid, identify and clear the blocking block first, and avoid undoing prior progress by re-stacking blocks you just moved.', 'When When multiple objects must be relocated to a target room and both hands can carry one object each.: Before each move, verify your carried state and use check-valid-actions after any invalid attempt; then carry one object per hand, move to the destination, drop the objects that belong there, and continue to the remaining target room rather than retrying the same invalid action.', "When When an object is already being carried in one hand and must be relocated to another room, while the other hand holds a second object.: After a pickup succeeds, do not retry picking that same object with the same hand; instead move to the destination room and drop it, then return for the remaining object. Run check-valid-actions after any invalid action to confirm the object's carried state before acting.", "Act directly: output exactly ONE concrete executable action per turn. Do not output 'think:' steps; if you are unsure which actions are valid, output 'check valid actions'."]}
